> Here’s a self-contained plan for the **temple raid session**, tuned for a 6‑year‑old, with simple structure, 2–3 rooms, monsters, a boss cleric, and a clear hook for later adventures (including dragonborn).
> 
> I’ll assume:
> - Ekemon: level 2 fighter (whip + trident).
> - Two pirate allies: level 2-ish (you can just treat them as “Bandit” or “Thug” stat blocks and fudge as needed).
> - Goal of the session:  
>   - Hit the temple around noon.  
>   - Have 2 short combats + 1 boss.  
>   - Drop a clear hint about where dragonborn are from and set up a future dungeon (the Sunken Titan Temple).
> 
> You can run all of this in about an hour by trimming descriptions and maybe skipping the optional room if time is short.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Big Picture: The Temple of the Ember Dragon
> 
> **What the pirates want:**  
> The pirates have heard that this temple keeps **gold offerings** and a **magical relic** tied to an ancient “fire dragon” or “Titan of Flame.” They want loot.
> 
> **What the temple really is:**  
> - A small, old shrine dedicated to a **fire‑dragon deity** (or proto‑Titan) worshipped long ago.  
> - The local villagers barely understand it; they just keep the rituals going.  
> - Deep lore: this same cult once interacted with **dragonborn from the Redclaw Peaks**.
> 
> **What Ekemon can get out of it:**
> - Gold/loot.  
> - A **Titan Relic seed item** (e.g., a bracer or amulet) that will later grow in power in the Sunken Titan Temple.  
> - A **clear clue** about dragonborn and “Redclaw Peaks / Redclaw” to reinforce his idea.  
> - Optional: a **recurring NPC** (young acolyte survivor, or the boss cleric escaping) who can reappear later.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Structure Overview (2–3 Rooms)
> 
> 1. **Outside / Entry – The Burning Steps**  
>    - Optional quick combat vs. animated temple guardians or bandit defenders.
> 2. **Room 1 – The Hall of Ember Statues**  
>    - Simple trap/puzzle + a small monster fight.
> 3. **Room 2 – Inner Sanctum / Boss**  
>    - Boss cleric + one monster or guard.  
>    - Titan Relic + dragonborn clue discovered here.
> 
> You can run all 3, or skip Room 1 if time is tight and jump straight to the boss.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## NPC & Monster Simplifications (for quick play)
> 
> To keep things easy:
> 
> - **Pirate Allies (2):**  
>   - AC: 12  
>   - HP: 11 each  
>   - Attack: Scimitar +4 to hit, 1d6+2 damage  
>   - They don’t have special abilities, just swing and maybe take the Help action if you want.
> 
> - **Low-level guardians (Room 1):** 2 **Guardians of Ember**  
>   - Use **Guard** stats (AC 16, HP 11, spear +3 to hit, 1d6+1).  
>   - Flavor them as glowing, half-stone, half-fire temple warriors.
> 
> - **Boss Cleric: “High Ember Acolyte Seryn”**  
>   - Use **Acolyte** or **Cultist** stats with a bit more HP (say 18–20 HP).  
>   - AC: 12–13 (robes).  
>   - Attacks:
>     - Fire Bolt (ranged spell, +4 to hit, 1d10 fire)  
>     - Staff (melee, +3 to hit, 1d6+1 bludgeoning)  
>   - Spells (just describe effects; don’t stress mechanics):
>     - Once per fight: *Burning Hands* (a short-range cone, Dex save or 2d6 fire; on success 1d6).  
>     - Once per fight: *Healing Word* on herself or ally (heal 1d4+3).
> 
> - **Boss Monster Ally:** 1 **Small Fire Elemental / Ember Spirit**  
>   - Think of it as a “flaming dog” or “little fire dragon spirit.”  
>   - AC: 13  
>   - HP: 14  
>   - Attack: Flame Slam +4 to hit, 1d6+2 fire damage.  
> 
> Fudge rolls as needed to keep Ekemon feeling powerful but at some risk.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Scene 0: Approaching the Temple (2–5 minutes)
> 
> At high noon, the pirates send Ekemon + two pirates to the temple.
> 
> **Describe:**
> 
> > The sun is high and hot as you and your two pirate “friends” walk up a dusty path through palm trees and scrubby bushes. Ahead, you see old stone steps leading up to a small temple built into a rocky hill. Smoke curls from small braziers at the entrance. You hear shouting from the village behind you as the rest of the crew attacks the houses.
> 
> Give 2–3 clear options:
> 
> - “Do you:
>   1. Charge straight up the stairs,
>   2. Sneak around the side to peek in,
>   3. Or stop to see if anyone is guarding the entrance?”
> 
> Whatever he chooses, you can introduce:
> 
> - Two robed **acolytes** running out in panic (non-combat; they can flee), OR  
> - One **ember guardian** at the top of the steps telling them to leave (small 1-enemy warmup fight), OR  
> - No fight, just an ominous, quiet entrance.
> 
> If you want a quick warmup combat:  
> Use **1 Guardian of Ember** (Guard stats) alone. The pirates help; don’t kill them off unless it’s dramatically fun.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Room 1: The Hall of Ember Statues (optional but good) (15–20 minutes)
> 
> **Description:**
> 
> > Inside, the air is hot and dry. You walk down a short hallway into a long stone hall. On each side stand tall statues of armored warriors holding spears, their eyes set with dull red crystals. At the far end is a closed door carved with a picture of a dragon breathing fire over a mountain.  
> > The floor between you and that door has several dark, square tiles that look a little different from the others.
> 
> You can turn this into a very simple **trap/puzzle**:
> 
> - There are **safe tiles** and **trap tiles**.
> - The pirates look nervous: “Uh… boss… I don’t like those statues.”
> 
> Give him **obvious options**:
> 
> > “Do you:
> > 1. Just walk straight down the middle,
> > 2. Try stepping only on the lighter-colored tiles,
> > 3. Or poke a tile with your trident from back here?”
> 
> If he:
> - **Walks straight**:  
>   - Trigger the trap: one of the **statues comes to life** as a Guardian of Ember and attacks.  
>   - Or flame jets from the wall: Dex save to halve 2d6 fire (you can soften the damage).  
> - **Steps carefully** or **pokes with trident**:  
>   - Let him avoid or reduce the trap with a simple roll (DC 10–12 Perception or Investigation).  
>   - Maybe just one small flame burst (1d4) and then success.
> 
> Either way, end with **2 Guardians of Ember** animating from statues (use Guard stats). These are the combat of the room.
> 
> **Tactics:**  
> They try to block Ekemon while shouting about “defilers.” The pirates can each engage one, or both of them can Help Ekemon to give him advantage.
> 
> **Loot in Room 1 (optional):**
> 
> After the fight, among the broken stone and ash:
> 
> - A small **bronze fire-dragon token** (worth a few gold).
> - A wall carving of a **mountain range with a dragon silhouette above it**, labeled in old Draconic runes.
> 
> If he checks it, you can say:
> 
> > “You see faded letters under the mountain picture. Your pirate friend squints and says, ‘Huh… I can’t read these scribbles, but I once heard of a place called **Redclaw Peaks**, where dragons used to live. Looks kind of like that, eh?’”
> 
> That directly reinforces his “Redclaw” idea: **this temple’s dragon cult had contact with that region.**
> 
> ---
> 
> ## Room 2: Inner Sanctum – The Ember Heart (Boss) (20–25 minutes)
> 
> **Description:**
> 
> > You push open the carved dragon door. Inside is a round chamber lit by a ring of fire braziers. In the center stands a stone altar with a glowing red crystal set into it, shaped like a heart. Behind the altar is a robed figure with flame patterns on her sleeves: a cleric of this fire temple.  
> > She glares at you. “Pirates… you dare profane the Heart of the Ember Dragon?”  
> > Beside her, a small creature made of fire, like a dog made of living flame, growls and flares brighter.
> 
> This is **High Ember Acolyte Seryn** + **Ember Spirit**.
> 
> ### How to play the scene
> 
> Let Ekemon talk first if he wants:
> 
> - If he threatens: she’s defiant, calls him “little devil” and refuses to hand over the relic.  
> - If he tries to intimidate: you can let him roll Intimidation; on success she’s shaken but still fights (she’s protecting the temple).  
> - If he’s weirdly nice, she’s confused but still hostile because of the pirates.
> 
> Either way, this is your **boss fight**.
> 
> ### Boss Fight Setup
> 
> Enemies:
> - **Seryn (cleric)** – behind the altar.
> - **Ember Spirit** – charges at Ekemon or a pirate.
> 
> Tactics (kept simple):
> 
> - **Round 1–2:**
>   - Ember Spirit runs in and attacks in melee.
>   - Seryn:
>     - Round 1: casts *Burning Hands* if Ekemon + a pirate are in front of her in a cone; otherwise *Fire Bolt* at Ekemon.
>     - Round 2: *Healing Word* on herself or the Ember Spirit if one is badly hurt, or just *Fire Bolt*.
> 
> - **Later:**  
>   - Switch to staff melee if cornered or low on spells.  
>   - Shout dramatic lines: “The Ember Dragon will burn you all!”, “You can’t steal the sacred heart!”
> 
> Let the pirates help, but if Ekemon takes a lot of hits, maybe one pirate steps in and takes a blow (“No—urk! I got this one, boss!”) to keep the kid alive.
> 
> If Ekemon drops to 0 HP, have one pirate try to stabilize him or Seryn accidentally knock him out instead of killing him—then you can narrate a capture/escape. But ideally, let him win.
> 
> ---
> 
